Voting Unit (Unit A):
All full-time and regular part-time employees employed by the Employer, including
utility operators, mechanics, assistant superintendents, and superintendents;
excluding all other employees and guards and supervisors as defined by the Act

Included: All Staking Engineers, GIS Technician, Energy Services Technicians, and Energy Services Coordinators; 

Excluded: All other employees, confidential employees, guards and supervisors as defined by Act.

If a majority of valid ballots are cast for IBEW Local 1593, they will be taken to have indicated the employees’ desire to be included in the existing employee unit, consisting of lineworkers and meter technicians, among other classifications,  currently represented by the incumbent Union. If a majority of valid ballots are not cast for representation, they will be taken to have indicated the employees’ desire to remain unrepresented.

Included: All full-time and regular part-time O&M technicians, team leads, and maintenance helpers employed by the Employer at its Rock Falls, Illinois facility;

Excluded: All office clerical employees, plant engineers, professional employees, guards and supervisors as defined by the Act.

Others permitted to vote: The parties have agreed that administrative assistants may vote in the election, but their ballots will be challenged since their eligibility has not been resolved.  No decision has been made regarding whether the individuals in this classification or group are included in, or excluded from, the bargaining unit. The eligibility or inclusion of these individuals will be resolved, if necessary, following the election.

Included: All full-time and regular part-time Senior Distribution System Operators;

Excluded: Clerical employees, Guards, and Supervisors as defined by the Act, and all other employees.

If a majority of the valid ballots are cast for International Brotherhood of Electrical Workers Local Union 160, AFL-CIO, they will be taken to have indicated the employees’ desire to be included in the existing bargaining unit of employees currently represented by International Brotherhood of Electrical Workers Local Union 160, AFL-CIO, and covered by the Metro West Region Labor Agreement. If a majority of the valid ballots are not cast for representation, they will be taken to have indicated the employees’ desire to remain unrepresented.

Including:  All full-time and regular part-time housekeeping, food and beverage, front desk, and maintenance employees employed by the Employer at the Hilton Garden Inn Dubuque Downtown, located in Dubuque, IA; 
Excluding: All office clerical employees, professional employees, Houlihan's employees, sales employees, accounting employees, and guards and supervisors as defined in the Act.

Other Permitted to vote:  The parties have agreed that the classifications of food & beverage supervisor, front desk supervisor, housekeeping supervisor, and lead engineer may vote in the election but their ballots will be challenged since their eligibility has not been resolved.  No decision has been made regarding whether the individuals in these classifications or groups are included in, or excluded from, the bargaining unit.  The eligibility or inclusion of these individuals will be resolved, if necessary, following the election.

Included:  All full-time and regular part-time Distribution Service Representative I, II and Senior;

Excluded:  Professionals, managers, and guards and supervisors as defined by the Act, as amended.

If a majority of valid ballots are cast for INTERNATIONAL BROTHERHOOD OF ELECTRICAL WORKERS LOCAL 31, they will be taken to have indicated the employees’ desire to be included in the existing unit represented by INTERNATIONAL BROTHERHOOD OF ELECTRICAL WORKERS LOCAL 31, as described in its current collective bargaining agreement with the Employer effective February 1, 2018, through April 30, 2020.  If a majority of valid ballots are not cast for representation, they will be taken to have indicated the employees’ desire to remain unrepresented.

